Subject: Explanatory power using logistic lme4
Message-ID: <CAKpA2X9WBM_mNO2YTMUdfJpLCyNnJzALdp3fMviukEi6+MkwHg@mail.gmail.com>

Hi Ling-R,

I'm creating a series of models using lme4 and a categorical DV to model
the effect of various lexical variables on word recognition accuracy, and
then comparing those models using the anova() function. A reviewer has
asked me to include more discussion of how good the overall fit of the
models are of the data. That is, do the models account for the vast
majority or only a small fraction of the total variance in word recognition
accuracy? I know the challenges of trying to use pseudo R^2 with
categorical DVs and am not trying to explain how much variance each
predictor accounts for, rather, I'm looking for a way to contextualize the
absolute explanatory power of the full model.

Any thoughts?

Thanks,
Julia

